{title: 129 - As It Fell Upon a Night}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Jesus Christ}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[D]As it [G]fell [F#m]upon [A]a [Bm]night
[D]In the winter [C#dim]weather,
[Bm]Angels [A]bright [F#m]in [A]starry [F#m]height
[D]Began [F#m]to [A]sing [G]together.

Verse 2:
[D]Shepherds [G]sleeping [D]on [A]the [Bm]plain
[D]Woke to see [Em]the [C#dim]glory,
[Bm]All [A]amazed [F#m]they [A]stood [G]and [F#m]gazed
[D]And [Em]heard [F#m]the [A]angels' [Em]story.

Verse 3:
[D]Unto [G]you [F#m]a [D]child [A]is [Bm]born
[D]In a manger [C#dim]lowly,
[Bm]Humble, [A]He, [F#m]yet [A]born [G]to [F#m]be
[D]The [Em]King [F#m]of [A]Love [G]most [Em]holy.

Verse 4:
[D]Happy [G]angels [D]from [A]afar,
[D]Cease your singing [C#dim]never!
[Bm]In [A]excelsis [G]gloria!
[D]For [Em]ever [A]and [G]for [Em]ever.
